<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Three miners die in Western Areas accident.</title>
<headline>Three miners die in Western Areas accident.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three mineworkers were killed in an underground accident early on Friday morning at Western Areas Gold Mine, mine manager JCI Ltd said in a statement.</p>
<p>The men, part of a team rehabilitating and supporting a haulage on the 43 level, were killed in a fall of ground about 1,300 metres underground. The accident occured at 0200 GMT.</p>
<p>JCI said that a full investigation into the cause of the accident has begun.</p>
<p>Western Areas produced 4,391 kg of gold in the three months to end March.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
